## 2. Work out what "like for Serbian" actually means today
#
# WRONG TURN #1: there were two plausible readings and they lead to
# materially different work —
#   (a) widen the Vertex/Gemini Live bridge to ru (the Serbian *solution*)
#   (b) point ru's cascade TTS at a Google Cloud TTS voice
#       (ru-RU-Wavenet-A, literally "replace Tatyana with a Google voice")
# Serbian has had THREE answers over time (Google TTS, then Fish, then the
# Vertex bridge), so "like for Serbian" is ambiguous on its own. Resolved it
# by checking what Serbian runs RIGHT NOW rather than by asking:

grep -rn "VERTEX_SERBIAN_BRIDGE_ENABLED" .github/workflows/AWS-PROD-DEPLOY-GATEWAY.yml
#   -> {name:"VERTEX_SERBIAN_BRIDGE_ENABLED", value:"true"} is pinned on
#      PRODUCTION. So the live Serbian mechanism is the Vertex/Gemini bridge
#      -> reading (a).

## 3. Verify every precondition rather than assuming it

# Does Gemini Live actually speak Russian?
#   WebFetch ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/live-guide
#   -> 99 languages; `ru` AND `sr` both listed. Confirmed 2026-10-01.

# Is the Gemini voice for ru correctly gendered for Vitana (VTID-04445)?
grep -n "GEMINI_VOICE_GENDER" -A 40 services/gateway/src/orb/live/voice/persona-voice-gender.ts
#   -> Kore: female, Aoede: female, Charon: male

# What voice will a ru bridge session actually get? (read-only, live DB)
#   SELECT policy_key, value_json FROM decision_policy
#    WHERE policy_key IN ('voice.live_api.voice.ru','voice.live_api.voice.sr');
#   -> ru: {"voice_name":"Aoede","fallback_lang":"en"}
#   -> sr: {"voice_name":"Aoede","fallback_lang":"en"}
#   IDENTICAL. ru inherits a voice already proven on this bridge in
#   production, and Aoede is female -> no DB change needed or made.

# Is the CLAUDE.md watchdog-parity precondition satisfiable?
sed -n '335,365p' services/gateway/src/orb/live/session/live-session-controller.ts
grep -n "SESSION_TIMEOUT_MS" services/gateway/src/orb/live/config.ts
sed -n '17880,17905p' services/gateway/src/routes/orb-live.ts
#   -> cleanupExpiredSessions() + the wsClientSessions sweep both expire any
#      session idle > SESSION_TIMEOUT_MS (30 min) every 5 min, and NEITHER
#      reads the provider. A Vertex session is bounded like a Nova one.

# How much traffic would this actually expose? (read-only, live DB)
#   SELECT metadata->>'lang', count(*) FROM oasis_events
#    WHERE topic='orb.live.diag' AND metadata->>'stage'='greeting_sent'
#      AND created_at > now() - interval '30 days' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC;
#   -> de 866, en 258, sr 136, ru 18, fr 3, es 1
#   ru is ~7.5x SMALLER than sr, which is already on this bridge in prod.

