## 7. Two repo guards caught real problems — fixed properly, not loosened

# WRONG TURN #2: the VTID-03788 guard failed —
#   "AWS-PROD-DEPLOY-GATEWAY.yml: no single run: step exceeds 20,000 chars"
# My explanatory comment pushed the prod run: step 238 chars over GitHub's
# hard limit. Measured it, then CONDENSED the comment to a one-line pointer
# (the full rationale lives in the module header and backend.md) rather than
# touching the guard. Final headroom: 49 chars.
python3 -c "import yaml;d=yaml.safe_load(open('.github/workflows/AWS-PROD-DEPLOY-GATEWAY.yml'))
[print(len(s['run']),s['name'][:45]) for j in d['jobs'].values() for s in j.get('steps',[]) if s.get('run') and len(s['run'])>18000]"
